PHASE 16 — AI Teacher and Marketing Tools

Goal:
Build AI tools with strict preview, logging, and cost control.

AI tools:
1. Analyze Student
2. Plan Remaining Sessions
3. Prepare Next Lesson
4. Generate Homework
5. Generate Scenario
6. Generate Weekly Student Summary
7. Generate Article
8. Generate Article Cover Image Prompt

Global AI rules:
- Save prompt.
- Save response.
- Save estimated tokens/cost if possible.
- Save tool name and related student/article/homework ID.
- Enforce regenerate limits from settings.
- Output preview only.
- Never auto-publish.
- Owner must click Apply/Save.
- AI output status starts as draft.

Pages:
- /owner/ai
- /owner/ai/logs
- /owner/students/[id]/ai
- /owner/weekly-summaries
- /owner/cms/articles/generate

Generate Article output:
- Arabic title
- English title optional
- slug
- SEO meta title
- SEO meta description
- excerpt
- full article
- CTA
- target audience
- keywords
- suggested cover image prompt
- status draft

Weekly Summary includes:
- This week summary
- What went well
- Areas to focus on
- Suggested focus next week
- Engagement level: High/Medium/Low

Acceptance criteria:
- Owner can run each AI tool.
- AI output is previewed.
- Owner can apply/save draft.
- AI usage log records prompt/response.
- Regenerate limit works.
- Generated article is draft only.

Manual test checklist:
- Generate student analysis.
- Generate homework but do not apply.
- Apply after preview.
- Generate weekly summary.
- Generate article draft.
- Check AI logs.

Stop condition:
Stop here. Test this phase before continuing.
